1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,040
Video and sound, different lengths.

2
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:15,470
What exactly does -shortest cut?

3
00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:25,330
Video 5 s (125 frames). Tones 3 s and 8 s.

4
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:31,600
Two readers: ffprobe, and a full decode.

5
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:38,810
No -shortest: file 5 s, sound 3 s.

6
00:00:38,810 --> 00:00:44,220
Last 2 seconds silent. 125 frames.

7
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:51,040
-shortest -c copy: file 3 s.

8
00:00:51,040 --> 00:01:00,140
Video 73 frames, 2.92 s. Sound 3 s.

9
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:04,500
Re-encode + -shortest: 75 frames, 3 s.

10
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:07,610
Picture and sound end together.

11
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:16,530
No -shortest: file 8 s, picture ends at 5 s.

12
00:01:16,530 --> 00:01:23,660
-shortest: sound trimmed to 5 s. 125 frames.

13
00:01:23,660 --> 00:01:30,920
-shortest follows the shortest stream.

14
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:39,640
Not tested: other containers, 3+ streams.
